   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation\nto issuing temporary permits to certain fantasy sports operators",
    "basePrintNo": "S4815",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4815-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1402 & 1401, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4815\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in\nrelation to issuing temporary permits to certain fantasy sports opera-\ntors\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo enable certain fantasy sports operators to legally operate interac-\ntive fantasy sports contests.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Subdivision 2 of section 1402 of the racing, pari-mutuel\nwagering and breeding law is amended and subdivision 1 is amended to\nallow for additional interactive fantasy sports operators and the\ncollection of tax.\n\nSection 2. Subdivision 8 of section 1401 of the racing, pari-mutuel\nwagering and breeding law, is amended to clarify the definition of\nInteractive fantasy sports contest.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently in New York State, fantasy operators cannot obtain a temporary\npermit to operate interactive fantasy contests unless they were operat-\ning such contests before November 10, 2015. As a result, the fantasy\nsports industry and contests available to consumers have been stifled by\nthe outdated limitation of existing law. This bill provides a mechanism\nfor newer operators to legally operate interactive fantasy sports\ncontests and provides for a payment of taxes in New York State.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
